Map Display Issue Analysis

I've reviewed your code and found the root cause of the map display problem. The issue is with the map container initialization - the map div has a min-height set but the map container's height isn't being properly respected during the initial render.

The Problem

The map container structure is:

```html
<div class="map-container">
    <div id="map"></div>
</div>
```

When the map initializes, the container may not have a proper height calculated yet. The JavaScript sets:

```javascript
mapContainer.style.height = '500px';
```

But the #map div needs to have its height explicitly set or the container needs to properly manage the height cascade.

The Fix

Here are the key changes needed:

1. CSS Fix (Add this to your <style> section)

```css
/* Fix map container - ensure proper height cascade */
.map-container {
    height: 500px;
    background-color: #e9ecef;
    border-radius: 8px;
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    width: 100%;
    min-height: 500px;  /* Add this */
}

#map {
    height: 100% !important;  /* Force height to fill container */
    width: 100%;
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: #f8f9fa;
    position: relative;  /* Add this */
    min-height: 500px;  /* Add this */
    z-index: 1;  /* Add this to ensure proper layering */
}
```

2. JavaScript Fix (Update the initMap function)

Replace the map initialization section with:

```javascript
initMap: function() {
    console.log('Starting map initialization...');
    
    const mapContainer = document.getElementById('map');
    if (!mapContainer) {
        console.error('Map container not found');
        return;
    }
    
    const site = Utils.getCurrentSite();
    if (!site) {
        mapContainer.innerHTML = '<div class="alert alert-warning">No site selected</div>';
        return;
    }
    
    let mapData = db.siteMaps[db.currentSiteId];
    if (!mapData) {
        mapData = Utils.generateSiteLocation(db.currentSiteId);
        db.siteMaps[db.currentSiteId] = mapData;
    }
    
    if (window.map) {
        try { window.map.remove(); } catch(e) {}
        window.map = null;
    }
    
    try {
        // Clear container and set height
        mapContainer.innerHTML = '';
        mapContainer.style.height = '500px';
        mapContainer.style.minHeight = '500px';
        
        // Ensure the map div has proper styling
        mapContainer.style.position = 'relative';
        
        // Initialize map with explicit size
        window.map = L.map('map', {
            center: mapData.center,
            zoom: 13,
            zoomControl: true
        });
        
        // Set map size explicitly
        window.map.invalidateSize();
        
        // Add tile layer
        L.tileLayer('https://{s}.tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png', {
            attribution: '&copy; OpenStreetMap'
        }).addTo(window.map);
        
        // Add site marker
        L.marker(mapData.center).bindPopup(`<b>${site.name}</b>`).addTo(window.map);
        
        // Create map layers
        this.createMapLayers(mapData);
        
        // Force size recalculation after render
        setTimeout(() => {
            if (window.map) {
                window.map.invalidateSize();
                console.log('Map size recalculated');
            }
        }, 100);
        
        // Initialize editing after map is ready
        setTimeout(() => {
            MapEditor.initEditing();
        }, 300);
        
        // Recalculate on tab activation
        const mapTab = document.querySelector('button[data-bs-target="#dashboard"]');
        if (mapTab) {
            mapTab.addEventListener('shown.bs.tab', () => {
                setTimeout(() => {
                    if (window.map) window.map.invalidateSize();
                }, 200);
            });
        }
        
        console.log('Map loaded successfully');
        
    } catch(error) {
        console.error('Map error:', error);
        mapContainer.innerHTML = '<div class="alert alert-danger">Map failed to load: ' + error.message + '</div>';
    }
}
```

